{
    "background_story": "Julia was a gentle soul with a deep love for botany and the healing arts. She lived in a small cottage on the outskirts of a medieval village, where she spent her days tending to her garden and studying the properties of various plants. Bedstraw, with its delicate white flowers and sweet fragrance, was one of her favorites. Julia would often use it to make soothing teas and infusions, which she would share with the villagers to help them sleep and find peace. As her reputation as a skilled herbalist grew, people would come from all around to seek her advice and remedies. Julia's kindness, compassion, and knowledge of the natural world made her a beloved figure in the community, and her use of bedstraw became legendary for its calming effects.",
